# Listing issues and merge requests

`glab issue list` and `glab mr list` do not accept `--state`. These fail with `Unknown flag: --state`:

```bash
glab issue list --state opened
glab mr list --state opened
```

Open items are the default. `--opened` still runs and prints a deprecation warning; omit it.

## Issues

```bash
glab issue list                 # open
glab issue list --closed        # closed only
glab issue list --all           # open and closed
glab issue list --per-page 50
glab issue view 10
```

## Merge requests

```bash
glab mr list                    # open
glab mr list --closed           # closed, not merged
glab mr list --merged           # merged
glab mr list --all              # open, closed, and merged
glab mr view 12
```

- Pass status with `--closed`, `--merged`, or `--all`. Do not pass `--state <value>`.
- `glab issue list` has no `--merged` flag. Only `glab mr list` does.
